      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the product of the roots of the polynomial equation \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas relate the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots.\n\nFor a cubic polynomial of the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\), Vieta's formulas tell us that:\n1. The sum of the roots (taken one at a time) is \\(-\\frac{b}{a}\\).\n2. The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time is \\(\\frac{c}{a}\\).\n3. The product of the roots is \\(-\\frac{d}{a}\\).\n\nIn the given polynomial \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\), the coefficients are:\n- \\(a = 3\\)\n- \\(b = -1\\)\n- \\(c = -20\\)\n- \\(d = 27\\)\n\nUsing Vieta's formulas, the product of the roots is:\n\\[\n-\\frac{d}{a} = -\\frac{27}{3} = -9\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the product of the roots of the equation \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\) is \\(\\boxed{-9}\\).",
